# Docs freshness

When editing code in the mapped areas below, also review and (if needed)
update the listed docs in the same change. Do not update docs
proactively when no corresponding code changes.

## Code area → docs map (Backend)

- `app/core/auth*.py`, `app/core/rate_limit.py`, `app/middlewares/admin_security.py`,
  anything importing `dotsound_private_core` policy functions →
  `docs/ai-boundary-policy.md`, `docs/private-boundary-inventory.md`,
  `docs/private-core-dependency-policy.md`.
- `app/services/upload_service.py`, `app/services/file_validator.py`,
  import workers, `app/api/v1/complaints.py`, playback, recommendation
  services → `LEGAL.md`, `docs/legal/*`.
- `frontend/src/components/Icon/Icon.tsx`, `frontend/src/styles/*.css` →
  `docs/design-system.md`.
- `app/` top-level reshuffle, new services, new routers, new stack
  additions in `pyproject.toml` → `docs/project_context.md`.
- Anything that removes or renames a symbol imported from
  `dotsound_private_core` → `docs/private-core-dependency-policy.md`.

## Cross-repo variants

Files with the same name in Bot and PrivateCore
(`docs/ai-boundary-policy.md`, `docs/private-boundary-inventory.md`,
`docs/private-core-dependency-policy.md`, `docs/public-release-cut.md`)
are **per-repo variants**, not byte-copies. When editing one of
these in Backend, check whether the change affects the scope claims
in the peer repos and update their variants if it does. Run
`python scripts/check_docs_sync.py` before commit — it exits green
as long as no truly-identical doc drifted.

## Hard rule

Never put PrivateCore internals (provider names, model names, pipeline
stages, scoring weights) into any Backend doc. Use opaque language.
